  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support scale-up of preventive and curative Nutrition, WASH and Protection services with integrated response in El Nino-drought affected Machinga district in Malawi.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of this project is to support children&#x2019;s resilience during the current drought in Malawi in coordination with the WASH, Nutrition, and Protection sectors in the Machinga district. Under the WASH sector, UNICEF will work to reduce the risk of acute and chronic malnutrition by providing children with water, safe community spaces, and sanitary equipment to be used at home to optimize the use of nutrients and growth. This will impact 10,780 women, 5,183 children, and 2,400 persons with disabilities. Under the Nutrition cluster, the activities will include the screening of 119,165 children for malnutrition, treating of 5,183 children for severe acute malnutrition, and the counselling of 36,165 caregivers of children aged 0-23 months. This will target 155,330 people, including 35,442 women, 119,165 children, and 4,447 persons with disabilities. Lastly, under the protection sector the activities implemented will include the screening of children for violence abuse and neglect, and the sensitization of their caregivers regarding protection for children, GBV mitigation, and referral to protection services for those who are experiencing violence. This will target 181,245 people, including 46,222 women, 124,348 children, and 4,447 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
